// VEX Decrypter 6.0 — victim recovery tool generated by the operator panel.
//
//   vex_decrypter.exe [options]
//     --journal <path>   journal to use; repeat to merge multiple journals
//     --key <b64>        AES-256 key (default: embedded)
//     --key-file <path>  read the base64 key from a file
//     --check            verify every file's GCM tags, write nothing
//     --list             print journal entries and exit
//     --only <substr>    restrict to paths containing substr
//     --exclude <ext>    skip paths ending in ext (repeatable: --exclude .log)
//     --workers <n>      decryption threads (default: cores, max 8)
//     --force            overwrite an existing original instead of .restored
//     --log <path>       append a result line per file
//     --quiet            no progress output
//     --no-elevate       never request elevation
//     --no-pause         never wait for Enter
//
// The panel injects {{AES_KEY_B64}}, {{VID}} and {{C2_URL}}; when those are
// present the tool reports progress back to the panel.
